 "script": "Nineteen seventy seven. Something called out. Seventy two seconds of it. Then nothing, ever again. A radio telescope in Ohio. It could not steer. The Earth turned, and dragged the sky across its beam. For seventy two seconds, something was inside it. August fifteenth. Ten sixteen at night. One man on the night shift, and a printer. Paper came out of the machine. Six characters. One thousand four hundred twenty point four five five six megahertz. The hydrogen line. The frequency of cold gas. Six. E. Q. U. J. Five. Thirty times above the noise. He circled it in red, and wrote one word in the margin. Wow. They looked again. And again. For fifty years. Nothing. Not one repeat. Then in twenty twenty four, a candidate. A magnetar flare, hitting a cold cloud of hydrogen. A natural laser. Not a voice. It is still not proven. That is the problem. The best evidence that we are not alone, and the best evidence that we are. Seventy two seconds. Fifty years of silence."
